# Release signing — committed on purpose (owner's decision; private repo, see below).
# Original note: never committed. keystore.properties holds the passwords in plaintext, and
# the .jks itself is the one artifact needed to ever ship an update under this app's identity
# again; losing it (or leaking it into git history, which is forever) is unrecoverable.
*.jks
!app/alpineterm-release.jks
*.keystore
!app/debug.keystore
